1. Why the source is visible
   The source is published so that anyone can read exactly what the commissioner sends to and reads
   from a gateway before trusting it with one. Publishing it does not make it open source, and no
   right is granted except those stated below.

2. What you may do
   You may use the commissioner, as served by Adsum Networks at commission.adsumnetworks.com or as an
   unmodified local copy of it, to commission, inspect and maintain gateways that run firmware from
   Adsum Networks and that you own or are authorised to manage. You may read the source to understand
   and assess that use.

3. What you may not do
   Without a written licence from Adsum Networks you may not:
   (a) copy, host, publish or redistribute the commissioner or any part of it;
   (b) modify it or create a derivative work from it;
   (c) use it, or any part of it, with firmware that does not come from Adsum Networks;
   (d) use its source, or the gateway interfaces it reveals, to build a commissioning tool, firmware
       or service of your own or for anyone else;
   (e) remove or alter this licence or any copyright or attribution notice.

4. Hosting platforms
   Where this repository is hosted on a platform whose terms let its users view or fork public
   repositories, those terms apply only within that platform, and this licence grants nothing beyond
   them.

5. No warranty
   The commissioner is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including
   fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. Adsum Networks is not liable for any damage
   arising from its use, including damage to or misconfiguration of a gateway, to the extent the law
